  "id": "Compound::DB05294 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Vandetanib is implicated in the pathogenesis of multiple conditions, including bone cancer metastasis, nail abnormalities, and peripheral sensorimotor neuropathy, through a mechanism involving the inhibition of specific enzymes. The evidence suggests that Vandetanib may interact with Cyp3a4, an enzyme involved in drug metabolism, through a series of molecular interactions. The lowest common ancestor of the implicated entities—Vandetanib, Maraviroc, Propafenone, and Disulfiram—points to a class of organic molecules, reinforcing the biological relevance of the observed interactions. The binding of these compounds to Cyp3a4, as indicated by the evidence, implies a potential role in modulating drug metabolism, which could contribute to the therapeutic effects or adverse effects associated with Vandetanib. The integrated evidence suggests that Vandetanib may exert its effects through a mechanism involving the inhibition of Cyp3a4, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
